<original_transcript>
{{ transcript }}
</original_transcript>

<project_metadata>
- project_name: {{ metadata.project_name or "unknown" }}
- assumed_team_size: {{ metadata.assumed_team_size or "unknown" }}
{% if metadata.mentioned_technologies %}- mentioned_technologies: {{ metadata.mentioned_technologies | join(", ") }}
{% else %}- mentioned_technologies: none
{% endif %}- agreed_scope: {{ metadata.agreed_scope or "not yet agreed" }}
</project_metadata>

<resolved_tier>{{ tier }}</resolved_tier>
<detail_level>{{ detail_level }}</detail_level>

<estimation_under_review>
summary: {{ result.summary }}
confidence_pct: {{ result.confidence_pct }}
total_duration_weeks: {{ result.total_duration_weeks }}
total_cost_eur: {{ result.total_cost_eur }}
phases:
{% for phase in result.phases %}
- index {{ loop.index0 }}: {{ phase.name }} | {{ phase.duration_weeks }}w | {{ phase.cost_eur }} EUR
  summary: {{ phase.summary }}
{% endfor %}
</estimation_under_review>

<cheatsheet>
Already computed. Use these numbers; do not re-add phases or invent a rate band.
Phase shares (imbalance only if share_pct is greater than {{ facts.imbalance_threshold_pct }}):
{% for row in facts.phase_shares %}
- phases[{{ row.index }}] {{ row.name }}: {{ row.cost_eur }} EUR = {{ row.share_pct }}% of total
{% endfor %}
Rate band: {% if facts.rate_band_eur is not none %}{{ facts.team_size }} people × {{ facts.duration_weeks }} weeks × {{ facts.dev_week_eur }} EUR/dev-week = {{ facts.rate_band_eur }} EUR. Estimate {{ facts.total_cost_eur }} EUR is {{ facts.delta_vs_band_pct }}% vs that band (negative = cheaper).{% else %}team size unknown — do not flag unrealistic_estimate on rate grounds.{% endif %}
</cheatsheet>

Audit this estimation. Return a structured ``CriticFeedback`` per the schema. Be specific in ``field_path``.
